Dhananjay -> Technical Assignment – Task Management System

Position: Junior Full-Stack Developer (Fresher)
Technology: Angular 22, TypeScript, Node.js, Express.js, MySQL
Duration: 2 Days
Difficulty: Beginner to Intermediate

1. Assignment Objective

Develop a simple Task Management Web Application that allows users to create, view, edit, delete, and track tasks through an interactive dashboard.

The frontend must be developed using Angular, and the backend must expose REST APIs using Node.js and Express.js.

2. Functional Requirements

Module 1 – Dashboard

Create a dashboard displaying four summary cards:

* Total Tasks
* Pending Tasks
* In Progress Tasks
* Completed Tasks

The dashboard counts must be calculated from actual database records.

Module 2 – Task Management (CRUD)

Create Task

Create a form with the following fields:

* Task Title
* Description
* Assigned To
* Priority (Low / Medium / High)
* Due Date
* Status (Pending / In Progress / Completed)

All required fields must be validated.

View Tasks

Display tasks in a table containing:

* Task Title
* Assigned To
* Priority
* Due Date
* Status
* Actions (Edit / Delete)

Update Task

Allow editing task information and changing task status.

Delete Task

Provide a delete option with a confirmation message.

Module 3 – Search and Filter

Implement the following features:

* Search tasks by title.
* Filter tasks by status.
* Filter tasks by priority.

Filters should work without reloading the entire webpage.

3. Angular Frontend Requirements

Use Angular 22 with the following concepts:

* Standalone components
* Angular routing
* Reactive Forms
* Angular services for API communication
* HttpClient
* Basic Signals or RxJS for state handling
* Loading indicators and error messages
* Responsive user interface

Suggested Pages:

1. Dashboard
2. Task Listing
3. Add / Edit Task

Candidates may use Angular Material, Bootstrap, or basic CSS for styling.

4. Node.js + Express.js Backend

Develop the following REST APIs:

Method	Endpoint	Purpose
GET	/api/tasks	Fetch all tasks
GET	/api/tasks/:id	Get task details
POST	/api/tasks	Create task
PUT	/api/tasks/:id	Update task
DELETE	/api/tasks/:id	Delete task
GET	/api/dashboard/summary	Get task counts

Backend Requirements:

* Express.js server
* MySQL integration
* Proper API status codes
* Input validation
* Error handling
* Organized routes and controllers
* Environment variables for database configuration

5. Database

Create a MySQL table named tasks.

Field	Type
id	INT, Primary Key, Auto Increment
title	VARCHAR(150)
description	TEXT
assigned_to	VARCHAR(100)
priority	ENUM
due_date	DATE
status	ENUM
created_at	TIMESTAMP

6. Expected Deliverables

* Angular frontend source code
* Express.js backend source code
* MySQL database creation script
* README with installation instructions
* Postman API collection
* Application screenshots
* GitHub repository or ZIP file

7. Evaluation Criteria

Evaluation Criteria	Weightage
Angular architecture and components	20%
REST API development	20%
CRUD functionality and database	20%
Frontend/backend integration	20%
Search, filtering and dashboard	10%
Validation, code quality and README	10%
Total	100%

8. Submission Guidelines

Time Limit: 2 Days

Mandatory:

* Fully working CRUD operations
* Functional API integration
* MySQL data persistence
* Working dashboard with task counts
* Basic form validation

Not Required:

* Login or authentication
* Role-based access
* Cloud deployment
* Advanced UI animations
* Third-party paid services

Candidates must be able to demonstrate their application and explain their implementation during the technical review.